## Summary
The article discusses the rise of remote working, spurred by the COVID-19 pandemic, and emphasizes the importance of data protection in this new work paradigm. It highlights the need for compliance with regulations like GDPR to ensure data security remotely.

## Key Points
- Remote working surged due to COVID-19-related directives, making data protection more critical.
- GDPR guidelines are essential for securing sensitive data in remote work environments.
- Organizations must adapt data protection strategies to address challenges posed by remote work.
- The shift to remote work increases risks for data breaches outside traditional office settings.


